onsDepicts":2,"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["udaipursolarobservatory","udaipur"],"summary":"Located on an island in the Fateh Sagar Lake, the observatory is claimed to be one of the Asia's largest. The observatory was built in the year 1976 by Dr. Arvind Bhatanagar following the model of the Solar Observatory at Big Bear lake in Southern California. Please note it is not open to the general public. You have to take permission to enter the observatory.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Udaipur","names":{"de":"Udaipur-Sonnenobservatorium","ja":"ウダイプル太陽観測所"},"photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Udaipur_Solar_Observatory_01.jpg/1280px-Udaipur_Solar_Observatory_01.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Udaipur_Solar_Observatory_01.jpg/500px-Udaipur_Solar_Observatory_01.jpg","w":1200,"h":800,"author":"Ganesh Mohan T","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Udaipur_Solar_Observatory_01.jpg"}},{"id":"udaipur_sukhadia_circle","areaId":"udaipur","name":"Sukhadia Circle","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":24.60124,"lng":73.69085},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"udaipur_sukhadia_circle","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":1,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["sukhadiacircle","udaipur"],"summary":"A large roundabout in the city's northern suburb of Panchwati, on the road to Ranakpur and Mt. Abu. The centrepiece of the Circle is a large, three-tiered fountain just over 21 m high, with scalloped dishes surmounted by a wheat-ear motif, representing prosperity. Illuminated at night, it is now a well-known landmark.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Udaipur","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/04/Between_the_clouds.jpg","thumb":"https:/